From 5e0f817bf9f2d08535b7b169a6cd49b635bf94eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:06:29 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] kcm_animations: effect list scanned after the page is
 shown; Form page with Windows / Desktop / Popups and sessions

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). kwinrc [Plugins] <effect>Enabled, kdeglobals AnimationDurationFactor, KGlobalSettings
notify and the effect config dialogs are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry replaced by Kirigami.FormLayout (works on 6.8.3 too) with sections
  "Windows" (was "Window animations"), "Desktop" (was "Desktop animations"), new title "Popups and sessions" for the
  untitled other-effects group. Speed slider stays first, no title; its legend and help button kept.
- Each combo + Configure... is one new component, ui/AnimationRow.qml (same controls as before, icon buttons have
  Accessible.name; combos have a minimum width so rows align).
- "More effects settings:" row became a "More effects:" button "Desktop Effects..." using
  KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings("kcm_kwin_effects") (fixed label; no KService lookup). kcm.launchEffectsKCM() stays in
  C++ for compatibility; effectsKCMData() removed (it was only used by that row).
- Combos and effect check boxes are disabled until the list is loaded. Busy indicator after 150 ms.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_animations.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 12 rows ok, 0 lost.

Speed (cause from code, not measured):
- AnimationsKCM::load() ran EffectsModel::load() synchronously: built-in effect list, KPackage scan for JS effects and
  findPlugins for plugin effects (common/effectsmodel.cpp:373-380) before the page existed; the constructor also builds
  7 subset models. The page bound effectsKCMData() -> KService::serviceByStorageId synchronously (kcm.cpp, old line 102).
- Now load() reads only the small kdeglobals settings; EffectsModel::load() runs one event-loop turn later
  (QTimer::singleShot(0), guarded against double scheduling); the existing D-Bus areEffectsSupported call stays async.
  New property kcm.loading (cleared on EffectsModel::loaded). The KService lookup is gone. Caveat: if KWin returns a
  mismatching list, EffectsModel never emits loaded() (existing behaviour), so the combos would stay disabled.
- Numbers: before (build/bench/clean/before-slow.tsv, under load) 604 ms first frame at 0.5 CPU. After: pending,
  manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-019, HIG-020, HIG-047, HIG-058.

Not built yet (freeze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
